/// `linux-host`: what the Linux personality needs from a host that standard WASI does not
/// provide. Everything else comes from WASI 0.3 (`wasi:clocks`, `wasi:random`, `wasi:cli`,
/// `wasi:sockets` when the node's `net` feature is on); networking extensions belong to the
/// embedder, not here.
///
/// The run-time translation tier (a host-instantiated CPU engine core module on host-owned guest
/// memory) is not part of this package: it is `translate:jit`, in `crates/translate-kit/wit`,
/// which a node imports optionally.
package linux:host@0.1.1;

/// Read-only, immutable byte blobs: root filesystem images (uncompressed tar) and other
/// content-addressed fixtures.
///
/// Blobs never change while a node runs, so a guest may cache any byte it has read. Calls are
/// synchronous and cheap to retry; callers batch reads (the personality reads in large chunks
/// and never crosses this interface per guest `read()`).
interface blob {
    /// Why a read failed.
    variant error {
        /// No blob has this name.
        not-found,
        /// The range lies (partly) outside the blob.
        out-of-range,
        /// The host could not produce the bytes.
        io(string),
    }

    /// The size in bytes of blob `name`.
    size: func(name: string) -> result<u64, error>;

    /// Reads `len` bytes of blob `name` starting at `offset`. Returns exactly `len` bytes, or
    /// `out-of-range` if the range does not fit. The caller owns the returned list.
    read: func(name: string, offset: u64, len: u32) -> result<list<u8>, error>;
}

/// `blob`'s reads as little-endian 64-bit words (0.1.1). Between two components a list crosses
/// element by element (the canonical ABI's adapters copy in a loop, with no bulk path for
/// lists), so eight-byte elements cross about eight times faster than bytes: a node with its
/// image composed in reads its root filesystem through this. Hosts that pass bytes in bulk
/// (wasmtime's own linker, the browser's jco glue) keep serving `blob`.
interface blob-words {
    use blob.{error};

    /// Reads `len` bytes of blob `name` at `offset` exactly as `blob.read` does, packed
    /// little-endian into `(len + 7) / 8` words (the last one padded with zero bytes). The
    /// caller owns the returned list.
    read-words: func(name: string, offset: u64, len: u32) -> result<list<u64>, error>;
}

/// A component that serves images (e.g. one with an image compiled in, for tests and for
/// hosts without a blob store).
world image-provider {
    export blob;
    export blob-words;
}

/// What `wasmshim-linux-node` needs from `linux-host`.
world node-host {
    import blob;
}

/// `node-host` for a node composed with its image provider (`wasmshim-linux-node`'s `blob-words`
/// feature, 0.1.1).
world node-host-words {
    include node-host;
    import blob-words;
}
